course: dictionary
lesson: 1362
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning separately, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The words around the word are its clues.
explain: «Sam remembers the swimming trip: he was the only boy who wouldn't do the cannonball off the high board, and he felt awful.» Here a cannonball is a jump into the pool, with your knees tucked up to your chest, making a big splash. The swimming trip and the high board are the clues.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. A heavy metal ball fired from a cannon would not fit a trip to the pool, so the swimming meaning is the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cannonball» as a noun means a heavy round metal or stone ball that used to be fired from a cannon.
fact: «Cannonball» (informal) means a jump into a swimming pool with your knees tucked up to your chest, which makes a big splash.
fact: «Cannonball» (informal verb) means to move very fast and with force.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always check which one fits the sentence.
exercise: «Sam remembers the swimming trip: he was the only boy who wouldn't do the cannonball off the high board.» What is a cannonball in this sentence? | A ball of wool for knitting | A small round sweet | *A jump into the pool with your knees tucked up, making a big splash | A heavy metal ball fired from a cannon
exercise: In a pirate story, the crew fired a cannonball at the ship. What does cannonball mean here? | To move very fast with force | A jump into a swimming pool | *A heavy round ball fired from a cannon | A kind of bread
exercise: The puppy cannonballed across the garden. What does cannonballed mean? | To jump into a pool with a big splash | *To move very fast and with force | To fall asleep in the sun | To fire a cannon at the fence
test: In a science lesson, the class drops a cannonball and watches it fall. Which meaning fits? | A jump into a swimming pool | *A heavy round metal or stone ball | A round cake | To move very fast with force
test: Which sentence uses cannonball in the swimming sense? | The museum has an old cannonball from a battle. | *Lia did a cannonball off the diving board and made a huge splash. | The cannonball was fired at dawn from the castle wall.
exam: Which meaning of cannonball fits best in «Sam remembers the swimming trip: he was the only boy who wouldn't do the cannonball off the high board, and he felt awful.»? | *A jump into the pool with your knees tucked up, making a big splash | To move very fast and with force | A heavy round metal ball fired from a cannon
